meta {
  name: Numbers · Assign 10DLC campaign
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v2.2/numbers/:number/messaging-campaign
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  number: <number>
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
{
  "campaignId": "ABC123"
}
}

docs {
**Assign a 10DLC campaign to a number**
Enables the number for messaging on a 10DLC campaign. The campaign is verified first: it must be available to the authenticated account (created by or shared with it) and ACTIVE. The number is then enabled on the messaging path the campaign lives on -- path B synchronously (200), path C asynchronously (202, status "pending": the number is provisioned with the messaging provider, then routed; poll GET /v2.2/numbers/{number}/messaging). A campaign that is still awaiting carrier approval also returns 202 "pending": nothing changes until it is approved, then the number is enabled automatically. A binding on another path is removed. Campaigns still on path A are being migrated and are refused (409). Number must be on the authenticated account.

OperationId: `numbersMessagingCampaignAssign`
}
